<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aissó</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Aizo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aissó, or Aizo, was a Gothic noble of the Spanish March who rebelled against Frankish rule in 826. With support from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba</a> he seized strongholds in the region of Osona and ravaged the area around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girona">Girona</a>. The failure of the Frankish relief army led to the disgrace of its commanders in 828, and Osona was left largely deserted for decades.</p></div>
